es by tomorrow it will be the  majority of the cases and it's  increasing  time and sadly yes omicron is producing  hospitalizations and  sadly at least one patient has now  been confirmed to have died  with omicron to combat what he called a  tidal wave in cases the prime minister  announced a booster blitz promising that  everyone aged 18 and up could get a  third vaccine dose before the new year  it's part of a range of measures to  combat a surge in the more transmissible  omicron variant people must now wear  masks in most public places and work  from home when possible as part of the  government's so-called plan b  in france too the government has  announced measures in anticipation of an  omicron fueled sixth wave of covert  the first closures in months came into  force this weekend with the nightclubs  shuttered until at least january  in austria the mood is much more festive  after a three-week nationwide lockdown  shops and cultural venues like theaters  and museums have reopened  though the unvaccinated will still have  to stay home  covered cases here have plummeted paving  the way to a brighter christmas  but with the omicron variant spreading  rapidly around the world there is still  much uncertainty about what the future  holds
 

